docs(adr): rate-limit claim:approach to block prune-storm DoS (ADR-0038)

Adversarial review: 'Contest-driven dynamic pruning has no rate limit
on claim:approach events; an agent polling once/sec could prune any
claim in milliseconds.'

Two rate limits added:
  - Per-(session, target) cooldown: 300s default. One contest event
    counted per (originating session, target node) pair per 5 min;
    saturated agents can't farm pressure.
  - Global pressure cap: contest_pressure = min(distinct_sessions,
    24h_event_count). A single repeat offender can never push pressure
    past N_distinct_sessions.

Audit-trail: cooldown-suppressed events still get activity_log rows
for retrospectives.


